      "side": 1,
      "message": "The approach of listing the dependencies to propagate is a problem.\n\nEvery dependency propagates unless there is a specific reason and justification to not propagate a dependency.\n\ne.g. the dependency is a compiler for building the target and not part of the target, that\u0027s a reason and justification to not propagate.\n\ne.g. the dependency is a runtime-only dependency loaded at runtime but not used to build the target, that\u0027s a reason and justification to not propagate.\n\nOtherwise, every dependency has to propagate its license.\n\ne.g. suppose someone, someday adds a resource dependency that can include digital images, the licenses for those images have to apply to the built target unless and until someone provides a reason and justification to not propagate.\n",
      "revId": "906922a9a470dbffcdf26c00742f579ecfade29a",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    }
